From: termux <maintainer@termux.dev>
Subject: Remove per-process global sqlite3 log callback from rpmdb backend

The sqlite db backend installs a process-wide sqlite3 log handler
(sqlite3_config(SQLITE_CONFIG_LOG, errCb, rdb)) that dereferences
rdb->db_descr. This is a per-process global setting, but the callback
closure points to an rpmdb handle that may already be freed (use-after-free).
Any other sqlite3 connection in the process (e.g. the dnf5 history
database) can then trigger the stale callback on reused memory, causing
a SIGSEGV in dnf5 history list when the history WAL has pending frames.

Backport of upstream fix for rpm 4.18.2:
commit d018e756b72c18d30e7c9109a552b86889e75c99
"Don't muck with per-process global sqlite configuration from the db backend"

diff --git a/lib/backend/sqlite.c b/lib/backend/sqlite.c
index d538973..2627fa3 100644
--- a/lib/backend/sqlite.c
+++ b/lib/backend/sqlite.c
@@ -44,13 +44,6 @@ static void rpm_match3(sqlite3_context *sctx, int argc, sqlite3_value **argv)
     sqlite3_result_int(sctx, match);
 }
 
-static void errCb(void *data, int err, const char *msg)
-{
-    rpmdb rdb = data;
-    rpmlog(RPMLOG_WARNING, "%s: %s: %s\n",
-		rdb->db_descr, sqlite3_errstr(err), msg);
-}
-
 static int dbiCursorReset(dbiCursor dbc)
 {
     if (dbc->stmt) {
@@ -170,7 +163,6 @@ static int sqlite_init(rpmdb rdb, const char * dbhome)
 	 * the "database is locked" errors at every cost
 	 */
 	sqlite3_busy_timeout(sdb, 10000);
-	sqlite3_config(SQLITE_CONFIG_LOG, errCb, rdb);
 
 	sqlexec(sdb, "PRAGMA secure_delete = OFF");
 	sqlexec(sdb, "PRAGMA case_sensitive_like = ON");
